I think that dexterity does have a lot to do with it.  I have not
checked the source, but I think that whether you discovered the trap
previously has nothing to do with it.  This makes no sense to me.  For
that matter, how does a dart or arrow trap go off twice?  That is how
rogue worked, but it never made sense then either.  Also, why doesn't
nethack ask for confirmation before you walk back onto a previously
discovered trap?  (just a rhetorical question)  I have a compromise
suggestion on handling such confirmations: let nethack check your INT
stat first.  If it is above 3 it asks for confirmation.  :-)

